'''Roos Tarpals''' was a [[Gungan]] [[Gender|male]] who served in the [[Gungan Grand Army]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]] and the [[Clone Wars]]. Prior to the Invasion of [[Naboo]], he served as [[captain]] of a patrol in [[Otoh Gunga]]. After the [[Battle of Naboo]], Tarpals was promoted to [[general]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], he sacrificed himself to protect Naboo from being conquered by General [[Grievous]].

==Biography==
===The Trade Federation Invasion===
{{Quote|No' again, Jar Jar. Yousa goin to da bosses. Yousa in big doo-doo dis time.|Roos Tarpals to Jar Jar Binks|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
[[File:Captain_Tarpals.png|thumb|left|250px|Captain Tarpals at Otoh Gunga]]
Roos Tarpals was a [[Gungan]] warrior who served in the [[Gungan Grand Army]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. He was acquainted with [[Jar Jar Binks]], who was banished from [[Otoh Gunga]] because of his clumsiness. During the [[Trade Federation]]'s invasion of Naboo, Binks returned with two [[Jedi]] emissaries&mdash;[[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]&mdash;who had come seeking help to get to the Naboo. Upon arriving, Tarpals and a colleague, who were riding [[kaadu]], apprehended Binks. Tarpals warned Binks that he was in "big doo-doo" this time.<ref name="Episode I" />

Tarpals brought Binks and the two Jedi visitors before [[Boss]] [[Rugor Nass]], the ruler of Otoh Gunga. Master Jinn saved Binks from punishment by enlisting his services as a guide to bring them to [[Theed]], the capital of Naboo. Boss Nass reluctantly granted Binks clemency and sent him away. Later, Tarpals was present when the [[Monarch of Naboo|Naboo Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] [[Boss Meetup|convinced]] the Gungans and Naboo to put aside their differences so that they could defeat the Trade Federation invaders. As a reward for his role in bringing the Gungans and Naboo together, Jar Jar Binks was promoted to the position of [[Bombad General]] in the Gungan Grand Army.<ref name="Episode I" />

During the [[Battle of Naboo|battle]] on the Grassy Plains, Tarpals served under the command of General Binks. Despite fighting bravely, the Grand Army was outnumbered and forced to retreat by the Trade Federation's droid army. During their chaotic retreat, Tarpals saved Binks from being killed by the [[OOM command battle droid|battle droid commander]] of an [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|AAT tank]]. Shortly thereafter, both Tarpals and Binks were captured by [[B1-series battle droid|battle droids]]. However, the destruction of the orbiting [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]] disabled all of the battle droids, turning the tide of the battle in favor of the Gungans and their Naboo allies.<ref name="Episode I" />

===The Clone Wars===
====Battle of Mon Cala====
During the [[Clone Wars]], Roos Tarpals was present when the Jedi Master [[Yoda]] requested assistance from the Gungan Grand Army to aid [[Mon Calamari]] forces during the [[Battle of Mon Cala]]. A Gungan detachment led by the Gungan Representative Binks fought Separatist forces led by [[Riff Tamson]] alongside [[Clone SCUBA trooper]]s, Mon Calamari, and [[Quarren]] forces.<ref name="Gungan Attack">{{TCW|Gungan Attack}}</ref>

====Final stand====
{{Quote|How does it feel to ''die''?''"<br />"''Not die&hellip; sacrifice!|General Grievous and Roos Tarpals|<ref name="Shadow Warrior" />}}
[[File:TarpalsSacrifice-SW.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Tarpals sacrifices his life to capture Grievous.]]
As the Clone Wars dragged on, tensions between the Gungans and the Naboo led the reigning [[Boss]] [[Lyonie]] to offer to aid the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] by sending the Gungan Grand Army to invade the Naboo capital of Theed. Unknown to everyone, Lyonie was being controlled through an necklace by [[Rish Loo]], one of his ministers who was secretly working for the Separatist leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]]. Senator Amidala and the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] managed to remove the necklace from Lyonie. However, Rish Loo sent a squad of [[BX-series droid commando|BX droid commandos]] to attack them, and Lyonie was wounded during the assault. With Lyonie unable to call off the attack, Binks assumed the identity of Boss Lyonie in an attempt to call off the Separatist attack.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" />

Tarpals accompanied Binks when the fake "Boss" climbed aboard the [[C-9979 landing craft|Separatist landing ship]] to help "coordinate the attack." While Binks distracted the Separatist commander [[General]] [[Grievous]], Tarpals informed Amidala of the Separatist general's presence. When Grievous realized that Binks was an impostor, he pursued the Gungan outside the ship. Tarpals and several other Gungans surrounded the cyborg general and attacked him.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" /> Even with his battle droids deactivated, Grievous posed a significant threat,<ref name="Heroes of Naboo" /> and Tarpals was well aware that he stood no chance against the Separatist General.<ref name="The Separatists">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Separatists}}</ref> Soon Tarpals and Grievous were fighting each other head to head. As [[Skirmish on Naboo|the skirmish]] continued, Tarpals was mortally wounded but used the last of his strength to "shock" Grievous into submission,<ref name="Shadow Warrior" /> which caused the cyborg's internal systems shorted out, making it easy for nearby warriors to capture him.<ref name="The Separatists" /> Despite his death, Tarpals helped to defeat a Separatist plot to divide the Gungans and Naboo. However, the Naboo and Gungans were forced to release General Grievous when Count Dooku captured and threatened Skywalker's life.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" />

===Legacy===
Despite the fact that it cost him his life, Roos Tarpals accomplished something that not even the Jedi had done before: he defeated General Grievous. Though the Naboo and Gungan later exchanged Grievous for Anakin Skywalker, Roos Tarpals' sacrifice inspired his people to face an enemy that seemed unstoppable; and win it.<ref name="Heroes of Naboo">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Heroes of Naboo and Other Characters of the Galaxy}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Tarpals-leading-Gungans.png|thumb|left|250px|Roos Tarpals was a skilled warrior and leader.]]
A Gungan captain<ref name="Episode I" /> who went on to become the leading general of their Grand Army, Roos Tarpals was gravelly-voiced<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|general-tarpals|General Tarpals}}</ref> but loyal to his allies, willing to lay down his life to ensure their victory.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" /> Although he initially disliked the surface dwelling Naboo humans, he came to respect them after Queen Padmé Amidala's humble plea for help<ref name="SWE">{{SWE|characters|tarpals|General Tarpals}}</ref> that proved she saw the Gungans as equals.<ref name="Episode I" /> Well into the Clone Wars, Tarpals still believed in the friendship between the Gungans and Naboo.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" />

Even though Tarpals had needed to go through many annoyances caused by Jar Jar Binks, the captain served under Binks during the Battle of Naboo<ref name="Databank" /> Tarpals also appeared to have a friendship with Binks, and urged for the newly-promoted general to not give up.<ref name="Episode I" /> During the Clone Wars, the two successfully worked together.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" />

Tarpals was a Gungan male,<ref name="Episode I" /> who stood at 2.24 [[meter]]s (7 [[Foot|feet]], 4 inches) tall.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> He had orange [[eye]]s and his skin was purple and white.<ref name="Episode I" />

==Skills and abilities==
Tarpals was a successful military commander, serving as a captain in the Gungan Grand Army during the Battle of Naboo<ref name="Episode I" /> and as a result of his leadership and military tactics, was promoted to general. He was also effective at both armed and unarmed combat as well as cavalry operations.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Behind the scenes==
Tarpals first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], voiced by [[Steven Speirs]].<ref name="Episode I" /> In ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', he was voiced by [[Fred Tatasciore]].<ref name="Gungan Attack" />

